From: lagz0ne <15101444+lagz0ne@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 06:01:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 53/55] fix(db): apply migrations by version set

drizzle's migrator (0.45) applies a journal entry only when its timestamp is
later than the newest one recorded in drizzle.__drizzle_migrations. A database
that already ran a migration stamped later than entries merged ahead of it
(a branch, a fork, a patch series rebased onto a newer upstream) skips those
entries without a word and boots on a schema missing their tables and columns.

migrateBySet keeps drizzle's table, row format and journal order, so a
database drizzle migrated is read as is, but runs every entry whose timestamp
is not recorded, all in one transaction. This is how Rails
(schema_migrations), Django (django_migrations) and Flyway (outOfOrder)
decide what is pending. Both drivers (node-postgres, PGlite) use it.

tests/migrateBySet.test.ts builds a database that ran the newest-stamped
entry but not an older-stamped one before it: drizzle's migrator leaves it
short, migrateBySet applies it and is a no-op on the next run.
